Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on revising core Node.js concepts to strengthen backend development understanding. Key topics such as modules, event-driven architecture, asynchronous programming, and handling requests were reviewed. Attention was given to how Node.js manages non-blocking operations and interacts with server-side applications. This revision helped in reinforcing the fundamental concepts required for efficient backend development.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, there was a clearer understanding of how Node.js operates and handles asynchronous tasks. The revision improved confidence in working with modules and managing server-side logic. It also enhanced understanding of event handling and non-blocking execution. Overall, the session strengthened foundational knowledge in Node.js.
